    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability on the first attempt. The ASAN output confirms the exact bug:\n\n- **Heap-use-after-free** at `plist_free_node` (plist.c:331) reading `node->parent` (8 bytes) from freed memory\n- **Freed** at `plist_from_openstep` (oplist.c:853) via `plist_free(*plist)` \n- **Allocated** at `node_from_openstep` (oplist.c:811) when the unquoted string \"a\" was parsed\n\nThe 2-byte input `a=` triggers the bug because:\n1. `node_from_openstep` parses \"a\" as a string, sets `*plist` to the string node\n2. `plist_from_openstep` sees `=` after the parsed value, enters the \"strings\" re-parse path\n3. `plist_free(*plist)` frees the node but leaves `*plist` as a dangling pointer\n4. The re-parse fails (no value after `=`), and the error path doesn't reset `*plist` to NULL\n5. The fuzzer calls `plist_free(root_node)` on the dangling pointer → UAF",
